-- title:
--   Krull dimension one for the pole chart of the Igusa model
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\ell$ equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure, and let $A =$ `chartAlgInf N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of the full modular function field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` consisting of all elements of $F$ that are integral over the subalgebra $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[\,j^{-1}\,]$ generated by the inverse of the element `jFull N` (that is, the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$ in $F$). Then for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of the $k$-algebra $k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$, the localisation of $k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$ at $\mathfrak{m}$ has Krull dimension equal to $1$ (as a value of `ringKrullDim`, with $1$ read as a natural number). No hypothesis is imposed relating $\ell$ to $N$, and $k$ is not assumed algebraically closed.
--
--   This is the dimension half of the assertion that the special fibre of the chart of the Igusa model of $X_0(N)$ around the cusp $j = \infty$ is regular of dimension one at each closed point; the companion regularity statement [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isRegularLocalRing_localization_chartAlgInf_tensor`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isRegularLocalRing_localization_chartAlgInf_tensor) uses it, as do the fibre and flatness statements [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.not_isOpen_singleton_fibre`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.not_isOpen_singleton_fibre) and [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.flat_pi`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.flat_pi). The proof invokes the general criterion [`Subalgebra.ringKrullDim_localization_tensor_eq_one_of_irreducible`](thm.html#Subalgebra.ringKrullDim_localization_tensor_eq_one_of_irreducible) for a finite, integrally closed algebra over a polynomial ring in one variable over a principal ideal domain, together with transcendence of $j$, the principality of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, irreducibility of $\ell$ in it, and the finite type and integral closedness of the chart algebras.
-- source:
